o not block this current source correction. Do not replace that historical statistic with the later62/63 counts.\n\nExact private candidate `fe6070272f269fde7683696e4c46a331902ab88baac8c5cc93db7bddf9d0ec1b` changes only components, component assertion, notes and one appended history event; all original history, identity, aliases, roles and other fields remain. Ten literal source components deliberately remain ungrounded in this bounded candidate. This is not a conclusion that suitable child IDs do not exist; final composition must incorporate the separate exact child-identity reviews without approval transfer.\n\nAdditional exact target `CONT-NCMA-WATER-001` belongs here under TV-002/TV-003: before-owner SHA256 `709749bd7c83c38a09400fc1893885ead753847ff9d1cbbe4ec76b431d349738` gives `components[11]` distilled water1.0L_PER_L. The complete [official NCMA6 source](https://ncma.bigelow.org/PDF%20Files/NCMA%20Medium%206%20Wolfe%27s%20Vitamin%20Solution.pdf), PDF SHA256 `b7bbf28efb43cfee8476e83780a55d929e574f3f0b7479583926d927409b4615`, specifies eleven solutes per litre and water/filter preparation, but no numeric water quantity. Preserve the genuine NCMA phosphate-containing source claim. A separately retained NCMA assertion must keep water unquantified; the CB candidate already replaces the unbridged NCMA decomposition under TV-003. No separate NCMA owner is silently created or repaired.\n\n[JCM197](https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=197), [NBRC837](https://www.nite.go.jp/nbrc/catalogue/NBRCMediumDetailServlet?NO=837) and [NBRC903](https://www.nite.go.jp/nbrc/catalogue/NBRCMediumDetailServlet?NO=903) support the nominal ten-vitamin batch recipe now, including the listed water input and source-specific preparation. Perfect molecular/lot specification is not needed to document it. The remaining decision concerns only exact association with the more specific CB cyanocobalamin/concentration/X100 scope; generic B12 and a listed water input must not inherit that specificity. Section3 permits a reviewed explicit nominal convention with details retained; it does not justify duplicate source-number owners or infer equality/difference from missing details. Treat this as a bounded representation/applicability obligation, not a new human-only permission gate.\n\nAll eight cases,71CM occurrences,84KG holds and six exclusions remain accounted. The65-context upper bound is not blanket mapping approval; exact aliases, child bindings, roles and exports remain separate. TV-001/TV-002/TV-004 are not closed. Independent checks rehashed980packet members, reproduced3closed-schema validations and baseline/overlay partonomy2956, checked actual historical Git blobs and all71recipe pointers. Evidence: `.temp/all-unmatched-20261107/preflight/tenvit-continuity-triage-v1/assessment.json`; original W09 packet and reviewer identities are unchanged. No maintained application occurred.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6719499726/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null,"pin":null}